> ### **AI and Genetic Research**
> 
> Recent advances in artificial intelligence, particularly in the genetics arena, have led to significant developments in variant effect prediction. AlphaGenome, a cutting-edge deep learning model, demonstrates how AI can enhance our ability to understand complex genomic sequences. This model, which processes vast 1-Mb DNA sequences, provides unparalleled accuracy in predicting functional genomic tracks and variant effects. Its success reflects a potential shift toward more comprehensive genomic analysis, suggesting future applications in personalized and precision medicine ([80718](#)).
> 
> The implications extend beyond genomic analytics. Insights gathered from AI models can help design targeted therapies, alleviate disease burdens, and promote preventive healthcare practices, aligning with global sustainability goals. As these tools become more integrated into healthcare system frameworks, the challenge will be ensuring equitable access and ethical applications across diverse global contexts.
